# NO KEY MATERIAL IS EVER COMMITTED.
#
# generate-certificates.sh is the source of truth for every certificate, key and store in this
# directory; the artifacts it produces are local, disposable and — in the case of the key — secret.
# Ignoring them by pattern rather than by name means a future addition (a client bundle) is covered
# the moment it appears, instead of the first time someone remembers to add it here.
#
# The ONE committed file besides the script is sample-idp-trust.properties: configuration that binds
# the `sample-idp` trust profile to the generated truststore. It names paths, carries no key material,
# and matches none of the patterns below.
*.crt
*.key
# Covers the generated sample-idp truststore and the script's own intermediate keystore, including a
# run interrupted before cleanup.
*.p12
